      "body": "## Overview\n\nReject dynamic speculative-decoding schedules with `ngram_gpu` during\nconfiguration.\n\n`ngram_gpu` currently requires the runtime speculative-token count to equal\nits configured maximum. Dynamic schedules can select a smaller value,\nincluding zero, causing an assertion failure that terminates the engine and\nfails every in-flight request.\n\nFixes #60981.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Replaces the runtime `NgramProposerGPU` assertion failure with an actionable\n  configuration error.\n- Prevents unsupported dynamic `ngram_gpu` schedules from reaching live GPU\n  inference.\n- Preserves existing static `ngram_gpu` and CPU `ngram` configurations.\n- Directs users to remove the dynamic schedule or use CPU `ngram`.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_config.py \\\n  -k 'ngram_gpu_rejects_dynamic_speculative_decoding or ngram_methods_accept_static_speculative_decoding' \\\n  -q\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```text\n3 passed, 439 deselected\n```\n\nRepository checks:\n\n```bash\nPRE_COMMIT_HOME=.pre-commit-cache .venv/bin/pre-commit run \\\n  --files vllm/config/speculative.py tests/test_config.py\ngit diff --check upstream/main...HEAD\n```\n\nAll applicable pre-commit hooks passed, including Ruff, formatting, mypy,\nSPDX, test tethering, and configuration validation. `git diff --check` also\npassed.\n\nThe original CUDA serving failure was not rerun locally because this\nenvironment has no supported NVIDIA GPU. The issue includes an A100 reproducer;\nthis PR tests the same configuration at the new validation boundary. No model\nevaluation is needed because the change rejects an unsupported configuration\nand does not alter model outputs or supported decoding behavior.\n\n## Details\n\nThe dynamic speculative-decoding scheduler can choose a per-batch draft length\ndifferent from `num_speculative_tokens`. The CPU n-gram proposer supports this\nby accepting values less than or equal to its configured maximum. The GPU\nproposer currently requires exact equality:\n\n```python\nassert num_speculative_tokens == self.k\n```\n\nWhen a dynamic schedule changes the draft length—for example, from `K=4` to\n`K=0` above 16 concurrent requests—the assertion terminates the engine instead\nof producing a configuration error.\n\nThis change adds validation to `SpeculativeConfig` so the unsupported\ncombination fails before the engine begins serving traffic:\n\n- `ngram_gpu` with a dynamic schedule: rejected with an actionable error.\n- `ngram_gpu` with a static draft length: unchanged.\n- CPU `ngram`: unchanged.\n\nSupporting variable K in the GPU proposer would require separate kernel and\noutput-shape work. This PR intentionally provides the smaller safety fix\ndescribed in #60981 without changing GPU decoding semantics.\n\nI reviewed #60981, its comments, linked development, and open PR searches using\nthe issue number and relevant keywords. I found no open PR implementing this\nvalidation or variable-K support for `NgramProposerGPU`.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\nAI assistance was used to investigate the issue, implement the validation, and\nprepare tests. The human submitter reviewed the changes and validation results.\n",
